WEBVTT

00:00:02.150 --> 00:00:03.520
It has gone as planned.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:07.900
You and Éléonore are tied by
a tight bond now.

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.490
So this is a game of bonds.

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:16.410
Either I download myself into you
and obtain that bond.

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.290
Or you come and take Éléonore back.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.630
I'll be waiting. You'd better come!

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.670
Let it bloom or let it wither

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:30.630
The setting sun ignites the horizon

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.390
And the gears turn

00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:48.190
When the horn blows, the flames dance

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:51.070
The story waits for no-one

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.950
Off they go, the gears are churning

00:00:54.110 --> 00:00:57.330
A red past chases after you

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.540
The jester's smile

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.410
What's behind the mask?

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:05.250
You can't erase the scars

00:01:05.420 --> 00:01:08.210
No matter how they burn

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:11.050
Let it bloom or let it wither

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.010
The setting sun ignites the horizon

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:19.680
Alone in the depths of the night

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:23.730
Let out a cry that can cut through fate

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:26.310
That's the cue to begin

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:30.230
The curtain is rising, it's time to dance

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.070
Everybody sheds tears at the end

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.950
So hold them in now and keep going

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:41.660
Until the day the curtain falls

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:47.130
The gears will keep turning

00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:58.510
#21 Silver goddess

00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:03.520
Master Shoji protected our village
for many years.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:07.560
We will pray for his soul here
for eternity.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:10.820
Grandpa...

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:14.490
Protect Éléonore for me.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.070
Don't worry.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:23.080
I'll protect Shirogane. I will.

00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:26.830
I'm sorry.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:30.250
I mistook you for Sadayoshi...

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:33.340
I was about to make a grave mistake.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.340
That's okay. How badly are you hurt?

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:40.720
I'll be fine.
Although it was a hard blow.

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:42.180
Masaru!

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:47.100
There you are! You had us worrying.

00:02:47.390 --> 00:02:49.810
What the heck? What happened here?

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:51.810
Did Shirogane find you?

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:57.530
I'm sorry.
Shirogane tried to protect me and...

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:00.450
And what? What happened?

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.240
But don't worry.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:07.330
I will save her.

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:10.920
Hey, what do you mean, save?

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:13.420
Shouldn't we go with you?

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:18.220
You can't.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:20.180
It's too dangerous.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.350
It's come.

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:31.850
ZONAPHA syndrome.

00:03:32.310 --> 00:03:34.360
Huh? But why?

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.660
To the dying humankind.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.960
How do you feel?

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.460
I am Deus.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:57.630
The god who brings an end to all life,
known to you as Faceless.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:03:59.470
Who the heck is that?

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:04.010
I love ancient Greek tragedies.

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.720
Especially those by Euripides.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:10.690
The ones that end
with a goddess appearing in the sky.

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:17.190
So I've decided to give you a goddess
for your finale.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.070
Can you see her?

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.860
What the heck?

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.780
Impossible...

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:32.750
She's Artemis, and her arrival heralds
the conclusion to your tragedy.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:37.170
As you may have guessed,
I gave you that sickness.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:40.420
There is no way for you to cure it.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:43.180
But listen here.

00:04:43.630 --> 00:04:45.550
You don't have to worry.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:49.680
Because every human on earth
is going to die.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.860
My silver goddesses are now flying
all over the world,

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:00.690
blowing the biblical trumpets
of the apocalypse.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:02.860
How do you like it?

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:18.840
How could this be happening?

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:28.470
Masaru...?

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.310
Don't.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.810
Please don't look at me.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:43.650
Faceless...

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.610
Masaru...!

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:47.570
Guri-pon.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:51.540
The puppet we were riding on
is in that truck, right?

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.000
Yes, I think so.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.660
Masaru.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:06:00.290
But why are we not infected
with that ZONAPHA thing?

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:03.670
Because you spent a lot of time
with Éléonore.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.930
She was born with immunity
against ZONAPHA.

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:10.720
It probably rubbed off on you.

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:13.560
Masaru.

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:15.140
He's flying!

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:19.360
Now, I mustn't let Masaru go alone.

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.020
Mr. Guy.

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.530
I have a favor to ask you.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:29.620
Faceless...
I'll never forgive you for this.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:33.580
People aren't yours to take.
And neither is the world!

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.700
Damn you!

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.460
You spread ZONAPHA syndrome!

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:58.520
I forgot to tell you,
but the goddesses are not solid entities.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:04.690
They're just clouds of
the ZONAPHA pathogen.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:08.570
A dust-sized automaton called Apollyon.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:13.200
These are what's causing you all
this suffering.

00:07:19.420 --> 00:07:20.420
Damn it.

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:24.170
Let's chase after Faceless, Masaru.

00:07:24.460 --> 00:07:25.590
Guy.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.470
And Lise?

00:07:28.090 --> 00:07:30.720
She implored me to take her with me.

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:32.720
Please, Masaru.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.720
I won't get in your way.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.140
I'll be of help to you!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.900
The legendary Guy,
the destroyer of 200 automata.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.780
Amazing how you dodged
my Cupid's Arrow.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:56.290
But you are going to die here.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:08:00.620
Only that boy there is allowed
to chase Lord Faceless.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.960
You go on. He only wants me.

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:07.800
Save Éléonore and the world for me.

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:10.130
Be careful.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:14.970
Now then.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:19.730
I've had my eyes on you as you're
an outstandingly beautiful shirogane.

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:22.140
What an honor.

00:08:22.520 --> 00:08:25.690
I'd rather hear that from
a human woman, though.

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:41.160
My body...
I can't move like my usual self yet.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.400
I am ashamed of myself.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:11.110
Let me tell you what I hate.

00:09:11.740 --> 00:09:14.360
Those wrinkles you humans have.

00:09:14.740 --> 00:09:17.450
Don't you think they're just so ugly?

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.410
But look at me.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.910
I have a beautiful face,
not one single wrinkle.

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.670
Guy, you're the second
most beautiful being after me.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:33.550
It's too bad.

00:09:33.840 --> 00:09:37.470
I wanted to turn you into an automaton
and make you my partner.

00:09:38.550 --> 00:09:40.930
Thanks, but that would never happen.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.730
Goodbye, Guy.

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:02.410
Narumi.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:04.200
How strange.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:07.920
I had a feeling you'd appear soon.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.920
There's no time to talk now.
You know why.

00:10:12.670 --> 00:10:14.880
The world is in danger. Let's go.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:19.390
-Go where?
-To where I first met you.

00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:21.720
The ZONAPHA Syndrome Research Institute.

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:31.230
Cupidia, your face...

00:10:31.690 --> 00:10:35.650
It's covered in the wrinkles
you abhor so much.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:41.240
What? A machine that can treat ZONAPHA?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:44.870
Yeah, they call it Harry.
Fou developed it.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:46.620
Fou, the jester.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:48.080
According to him...

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:54.760
You are all strong. You lived through
the war against the Midnight Circus.

00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:57.970
Now, I must ask you to do something.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.550
After years of research,

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:07.940
a machine to drive out the Apollyon bugs
that cause ZONAPHA has been completed.

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.060
What?

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:11.440
Can it cure ZONAPHA?

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:12.770
Yes.

00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:17.950
But I can't contact the people
who developed it.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:22.530
I don't know what happened to
the only test machine, either.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:23.870
An automata attack?

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:25.910
I'm afraid so.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:31.130
I need you all to go and protect Harry,
the completed machine.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.920
It's at
the ZONAPHA Syndrome Research Institute.

00:11:36.170 --> 00:11:38.970
Fou decided we'd need your help, too.

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.890
You've been there before many times.

00:11:42.340 --> 00:11:45.470
But I was against it.
After that plane crash...

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:49.640
You didn't even let me know
that you were alive.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.480
So that's why you punched me.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:55.900
You were worried about me.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:57.690
Yeah right!

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:05.160
Good, good.

00:12:05.530 --> 00:12:08.040
Once I get rid of every single human,

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:11.500
Éléonore won't fall in love with another.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:15.380
Nor will anybody get in our way.

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:19.510
Sir.

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:21.430
Lord Faceless.

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:22.930
Yeah?

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:26.680
May I ask you a question?

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:29.680
Say it, Colombine.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:36.320
Why are we three
of the Quatre Pionniers here?

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:42.530
We were defeated by the shiroganes
in the Sahara.

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:47.830
But you gathered us up.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:49.910
And fixed us.

00:12:51.210 --> 00:12:52.460
Would you rather I hadn't?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.420
No, all we feel is gratitude.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:59.550
But we do not understand
your intention, dear Creator.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:04.300
You've created more new puppets.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:08.560
Yet, why do you still
let us stay by your side?

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:14.390
Because it's funny.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.150
Funny, sir?

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:24.070
Yeah, you all make me laugh.

00:13:24.450 --> 00:13:27.910
You didn't realize that Doll Francine
had disappeared long ago.

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:32.040
And you served that fake puppet
like your queen.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:37.040
You're funny, you all are a joke.

00:13:57.100 --> 00:14:02.320
We've carried all the sick people inside.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:04.440
Good, we're done too.

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:09.450
But that Masaru, using that weird puppet
to fly through the sky.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:12.200
I'm amazed he could do that.

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.200
Well, yeah but...

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:18.750
Amazing as that is, he can't do this
all by himself.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:21.300
I don't know.

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:24.970
He might have it in him.

00:14:27.010 --> 00:14:30.350
One thing's for sure.
He isn't a boy anymore.

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.470
He's a man.

00:14:39.650 --> 00:14:42.320
Um, Lise?

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:46.190
Could you tell me why
you followed me here?

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.320
Yes...

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:51.620
I think I've told you before.

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.910
That my sister and I
were wild beast tamers,

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:57.870
until she was killed
by a tiger called Beast.

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:01.290
Yeah, I remember.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:06.840
After she was killed, I couldn't tame
those ferocious animals anymore.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:12.430
But I met somebody connected with Beast
at Kuroga Village.

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:18.980
My past about my sister and
how I can't tame wild beasts anymore...

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:21.190
I want to part with it.

00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:25.190
Parting with your past, huh.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:27.530
Thanks for telling me.

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:33.120
Now, let's toast the end of humankind!

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.830
Cheers!

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:47.460
Hello there, you old broken-down trio.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:53.140
This party is to celebrate the ruin of man
and the coming of Lord Faceless's love.

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.060
Having fun?

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:56.560
Yes...

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:57.890
Mr. Harlequin.

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:01.100
You two are such good little puppets.

00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:03.900
You've learned some respect.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:05.480
Here you go.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.530
What's this, Miss Diamantina?

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:10.200
You don't get it?

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:13.200
It's food for that woman we caught.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.540
Lord Faceless is so kind, isn't he?

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:20.410
Giving a puppet like you a job to do.

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:26.300
We're here to support Lord Faceless.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:28.760
So you don't have to worry about him.

00:16:34.340 --> 00:16:35.600
Narumi!

00:16:37.140 --> 00:16:38.430
Tom!

00:16:38.970 --> 00:16:41.600
It's been a while. I'm glad you're okay.

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:45.020
You've gotta help us,
the puppets invaded the institute.

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:46.360
Yeah, I know.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.570
What took you so long, Minghai?

00:16:48.860 --> 00:16:51.610
George and Ashihana
have already headed over.

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:53.240
Let's hurry.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:55.780
What a joke.

00:16:56.490 --> 00:16:59.790
A duet, against our big band?

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.960
We'll show you what real music is.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:07.290
This job is worth 20 billion.

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:09.590
Just comes rolling in.

00:17:11.170 --> 00:17:13.130
-They're here.
-Miss Mingxia.

00:17:13.430 --> 00:17:14.090
What?

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:19.260
Who would've thought a beauty like you
knew a brute like Narumi.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:23.980
-I'd love to have some wine with...
-Shut up, the fight's begun!

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:30.980
Miss Mingxia, care for that boy for us.

00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:35.240
Let's go.

00:17:39.530 --> 00:17:42.830
So, how do you like this bass?

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:48.790
Doesn't this perfect pitch feel great?

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:54.220
You foolish musician-wannabe puppet.

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:58.220
We can't make music.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:03.430
Why? Because both you and I
are nothing but metronomes.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.610
So tell me.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:20.700
What is it you wanted to do?

00:18:22.290 --> 00:18:23.700
Nothing.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:28.580
You bastards! I'll stop ZONAPHA syndrome!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:46.600
Hey, what's going to happen now?

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:51.440
For now, we have to find something.

00:18:57.820 --> 00:18:58.910
Don't look!

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:05.750
They're the soldiers who'd been
protecting this place.

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:09.620
But why are they dressed so strangely?

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.590
Tom, we shouldn't be here.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.050
Let's go.

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.260
I don't know about that.

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:25.770
I bet that you'll end up
the same way they did.

00:19:26.310 --> 00:19:29.270
-You did this!
-That's right.

00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:34.400
They all lost a bet to me, Gambler Jones.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:35.440
Little girl.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:38.610
"Little girl", my ass.

00:19:38.900 --> 00:19:40.240
The name's Liang Mingxia!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.320
No need to rush, girl.

00:19:42.620 --> 00:19:45.950
I'm a gambler.
There are rules to fighting me.

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:48.660
Run, Tom! Get away from here!

00:19:49.370 --> 00:19:50.460
Can't have that.

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:56.300
That's not fair!

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:59.510
You need stakes to gamble.

00:19:59.800 --> 00:20:03.510
You just have to win this bet
to save this boy.

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:06.600
Leave me, you have to go!

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:09.140
He won't let me go anyway!

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:11.390
Now, don't be so rude.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:15.320
I'm a gambler.
I don't lie or play dirty tricks.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:17.150
But...

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:20.320
I play with high stakes.

00:20:21.740 --> 00:20:26.870
Great, huh? These are body parts
I won from other automata.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:32.000
I've won lots of human parts too
since coming here.

00:20:32.290 --> 00:20:34.670
You've gotta get away!

00:20:36.590 --> 00:20:37.840
Fine.

00:20:38.260 --> 00:20:40.050
This game.

00:20:40.380 --> 00:20:41.510
I'm in.

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:52.270
Funny, huh.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:55.360
Lord Faceless is right.

00:20:55.770 --> 00:20:59.610
Lady Francine had been switched with
a fake puppet.

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:02.820
Yet we never suspected a thing.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:07.370
Not that again. Automata should accept
the truth as it comes.

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:09.660
No use crying over it.

00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:10.910
But...

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:14.330
Don't say it. We have a mission now.

00:21:14.620 --> 00:21:17.290
And it's to serve Lord Faceless.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:22.800
But the one who gave us
the power to think...

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:25.050
wasn't Lord Faceless.

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:26.850
It was Lady Francine.

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:31.350
Do come with me.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:35.190
Help me find a way to laugh.

00:21:36.230 --> 00:21:40.610
And if she exists no longer...

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:45.240
what is the use of our existence?

00:21:46.240 --> 00:21:47.570
There is none.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:54.910
Éléonore, here is your food...

00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.260
Who are you?

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:06.380
Lady Francine!

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:31.700
Avoiding the crowds, I walk in the dark

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:36.750
And wait with bated breath in the wings

00:22:36.920 --> 00:22:41.340
My expression is calm
while I scream inside

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:46.170
On the verge of being torn apart

00:22:46.470 --> 00:22:51.100
I dance and beckon you to join me

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:55.810
As a shadow swings across the stage

00:22:56.100 --> 00:22:58.940
I tell myself this is the last time

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:04.860
But I can't seem to cut myself free

00:23:05.150 --> 00:23:09.490
Too scared to stop for a moment

00:23:09.660 --> 00:23:15.250
My impatience hides
the cries of somebody left behind

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:23.380
Nobody notices the shadow
standing in the sudden rain

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:31.470
Somewhere far away,
a memory of you is saying goodbye

00:23:31.640 --> 00:23:39.310
I stand here watching,
no longer able to reach you
